        "original_id": "3410fec1-5369-57de-96ca-117c80063f44",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alvin Toffler, Isaac Bashevis Singer\n- Works: Future Shock, A Day of Pleasure: Stories of a Boy Growing Up in Warsaw, A Crown of Feathers and Other Stories\n- Awards: U.S. National Book Awards\n- Topics: Futurism, modern technologies, digital revolution, communication revolution\n\nFacts:\n- Alvin Toffler was born on October 4, 1928.\n- Alvin Toffler was an American writer, futurist, and businessman known for discussing modern technologies, including the digital revolution and the communication revolution, and their effects on cultures worldwide.\n- Alvin Toffler wrote Future Shock in 1970.\n- Isaac Bashevis Singer won a U.S. National Book Award in Children's Literature for A Day of Pleasure: Stories of a Boy Growing Up in Warsaw in 1970.\n- Isaac Bashevis Singer won a U.S. National Book Award in Fiction for A Crown of Feathers and Other Stories in 1974.\n- Alvin Toffler died on June 27, 2016.",
